From 1a6f6fe350e16c5e8b567a4986c08d7b84cf1192 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 01:18:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][Network] Projector control over the network: lens
 memory by the shape of the picture, picture mode by the signal

A group of its own in System > Display, "Projector control over the
network", off by default: the protocol (JVC D-ILA, Sony ADCP, Sony SDCP,
Epson ESC/VP.net), the IP address, the network password (kept as the
password of Kodi's web server is, shown hidden, never logged), "Test the
connection" (the model and the power state it answers), the lens memory by
the shape of the picture with up to three classes and their thresholds, the
hold before the lens moves during a video, the way back at the end, and a
picture mode for SDR, HDR10, HLG, Dolby Vision and 3D (the modes of the
brand chosen, or "Leave it as it is").

CProjectorControl runs on a thread of its own, started with the services
and idle while the setting is off; the player never waits for it. It
connects only to the address written, and an address outside the home
networks only once the user confirmed it when writing it. It reads the power
state first and sends nothing to a projector that is off; one that does not
answer, or is off, is asked again after 5 s, then twice as long each time up
to 5 minutes, and the user is told once while a video plays, not at every
try. After a lens memory nothing more goes to the lens for 10 s (a JVC
answers once its lens has moved). A command the projector refuses is not
sent again: it is said once, and in kodi.log with its answer.

While the lens memory is on, the bars of the picture are measured as for
subtitles in the black bars (the measurement and the level 5 block are
taken also with that setting off; subtitles go into the bars only with
theirs), and the renderer tells the control the shape of each picture
presented. The window system tells it the kind of signal twice a second.
The player information shows a row "Projector" while the control is on:
the lens memory and the shape it was taken for, the picture mode, or what
stands in the way. Strings in English, translated in Estuary (es_es, es_ar,
es_mx); the dialog of the player information for other skins is made again
from Estuary's (make-playerinfo.py).
