+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: help of videoscreen.hadesprojectorpassword (core #62711)
+msgctxt "#54711"
+msgid "Only where the projector asks for one. JVC: its network password, where one is set on it (the newer models need one). Sony ADCP: the ADCP password set on the projector. Sony SDCP: its community, four letters (empty: SONY, the one it comes with). Epson: its password for network control, up to 16 letters. It is kept as the password of Kodi's web server is, and never written to the log."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: label of videoscreen.hadesprojectortest (core #62712)
+msgctxt "#54712"
+msgid "Test the connection"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: help of videoscreen.hadesprojectortest (core #62713)
+msgctxt "#54713"
+msgid "Connects to the projector and shows what it answers: its model (JVC and Sony ADCP) and whether it is on. Nothing is changed on the projector."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: label of videoscreen.hadesprojectorlens (core #62714)
+msgctxt "#54714"
+msgid "Lens memory by the shape of the picture"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: help of videoscreen.hadesprojectorlens (core #62715)
+msgctxt "#54715"
+msgid "For a wide screen with constant image height. When a video starts, and when the shape of its picture changes and lasts, Hades selects the lens memory set below for that shape (for example memory 1 for 16:9 and 1.85:1, memory 2 for 2.35:1 to 2.40:1). The shape is that of the picture without its black bars: from the Dolby Vision metadata of the video (level 5) where it has them, otherwise measured on the picture, as subtitles in the black bars do. Store the memories on the projector first (zoom, focus and shift for each shape), and leave the view mode at Normal and the active area zoom off: the lens does the zoom."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: label of videoscreen.hadesprojectorlensnarrow (core #62716)
+msgctxt "#54716"
+msgid "Lens memory for narrower pictures"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: help of videoscreen.hadesprojectorlensnarrow (core #62717)
+msgctxt "#54717"
+msgid "The lens memory for the pictures narrower than the shape below (16:9, 1.85:1), and for the menus."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: label of videoscreen.hadesprojectorlenswidefrom (core #62718)
+msgctxt "#54718"
+msgid "Wide pictures from"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: help of videoscreen.hadesprojectorlenswidefrom (core #62719)
+msgctxt "#54719"
+msgid "Pictures at least this wide (their width for a height of 1) use the lens memory for wide pictures. 2.10:1 puts 2.20:1, 2.35:1, 2.39:1 and 2.40:1 there, and leaves 2.00:1 and narrower in the memory for narrower pictures. A picture has to become 0.03 narrower than this to go back, so that one at the edge does not move the lens back and forth."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: label of videoscreen.hadesprojectorlenswide (core #62720)
+msgctxt "#54720"
+msgid "Lens memory for wide pictures"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: help of videoscreen.hadesprojectorlenswide (core #62721)
+msgctxt "#54721"
+msgid "The lens memory for the pictures from the shape above (2.35:1 to 2.40:1, scope)."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: label of videoscreen.hadesprojectorlenswidest (core #62722)
+msgctxt "#54722"
+msgid "Lens memory for the widest pictures"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: help of videoscreen.hadesprojectorlenswidest (core #62723)
+msgctxt "#54723"
+msgid "A third memory, for the widest pictures (2.55:1, 2.76:1), from the shape below. None: they use the memory for wide pictures."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: label of videoscreen.hadesprojectorlenswidestfrom (core #62724)
+msgctxt "#54724"
+msgid "The widest pictures from"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: help of videoscreen.hadesprojectorlenswidestfrom (core #62725)
+msgctxt "#54725"
+msgid "Pictures at least this wide use the lens memory for the widest pictures."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: label of videoscreen.hadesprojectorlenshold (core #62726)
+msgctxt "#54726"
+msgid "Wait before the lens moves during a video"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: help of videoscreen.hadesprojectorlenshold (core #62727)
+msgctxt "#54727"
+msgid "How long a new shape has to last before the lens moves in the middle of a video. A film that changes shape (IMAX scenes) moves the lens at each change that lasts this long; a long wait keeps the lens still. At the start of a video the lens moves after 2 seconds. While the lens moves (a JVC takes up to a minute), nothing else is sent to the projector."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: label of videoscreen.hadesprojectorlensstop (core #62728)
+msgctxt "#54728"
+msgid "Back to the memory for narrower pictures when the video ends"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: help of videoscreen.hadesprojectorlensstop (core #62729)
+msgctxt "#54729"
+msgid "When the video ends, the lens goes back to the memory for narrower pictures, the shape of the menus."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: label of videoscreen.hadesprojectormodesdr (core #62730)
+msgctxt "#54730"
+msgid "Picture mode for SDR"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: xbmc/network/ProjectorControl.cpp
+#. Hades, the projector control: label of videoscreen.hadesprojectormodehdr10 (core #62731)
+msgctxt "#54731"
+msgid "Picture mode for HDR10 and HDR10+"
+msgstr ""
+
